dd1-cc57d113971d", "last_modified": "2019-08-20T21:57:42.009121", "metadata_modified": "2016-11-03T14:55:14.636253", "mimetype": null, "mimetype_inner": null, "name": "[SUPERSEDED] - Student outcomes measures based on the Grade 10 cohort : methodologies for rates calculation (March 2010)", "package_id": "395d6bc7-97dc-496c-b2ef-59b37234fe2a", "position": 3, "resource_type": null, "serialinformation_title": "", "serialinformation_uri": "", "size": null, "state": "active", "url": "https://open.alberta.ca/dataset/395d6bc7-97dc-496c-b2ef-59b37234fe2a/resource/2f52fad1-aa65-4fda-9dd1-cc57d113971d/download/2010-student-outcomes-measures-based-grade-10-cohort-revised-2010.pdf", "url_type": "upload"}], "tags": [{"display_name": "Grade 10", "id": "af58ec55-fa23-490f-bad5-1ecc63dc11b5", "name": "Grade 10", "state": "active", "vocabulary_id": null}, {"display_name": "examination participation rates", "id": "d1f91bde-23ba-429b-a948-7ad40b16d427", "name": "examination participation rates", "state": "active", "vocabulary_id": null}, {"display_name": "high school completion rates", "id": "bfb06a8e-c123-4fd7-b7f2-a10087d47481", "name": "high school completion rates", "state": "active", "vocabulary_id": null}, {"display_name": "high school transition", "id": "12675088-4d08-416a-b351-89b805489aed", "name": "high school transition", "state": "active", "vocabulary_id": null}, {"display_name": "student outcomes", "id": "fd05db3e-478b-4687-af63-de6b37616f10", "name": "student outcomes", "state": "active", "vocabulary_id": null}, {"display_name": "student outcomes measures", "id": "b2317ab7-4ea6-4704-80a1-eaf70170653a", "name": "student outcomes measures", "state": "active", "vocabulary_id": null}], "groups": [], "relationships_as_subject": [], "relationships_as_object": []}, {"alternatetitle": "", "audience": ["General Public"], "author": null, "author_email": null, "contact": "Corporate Planning", "contact_email": "", "contactother": "(780) 422-1963", "creator": ["Education"], "creator_user_id": "6911e9f1-653f-4051-a61e-f4b27245fb23", "date_created": "2015-05-11", "date_modified": "2018-03-28", "extent1": "", "id": "80968b69-c17e-4f26-92c5-eae3b7793ce0", "identifier": "", "isopen": true, "language": ["en-CA [default]"], "license_id": "OGLA", "license_title": "Open Government Licence - Alberta", "license_url": "https://open.alberta.ca/licence", "maintainer": null, "maintainer_email": null, "metadata_created": "2015-08-17T18:58:59.654001", "metadata_modified": "2026-03-26T17:34:38.812260", "name": "high-school-completion-rate-of-students-within-3-years-and-within-5-years", "notes": "This statistic reports the percentages of Alberta students in public, separate, francophone, charter, and accredited private schools who, within three and five years of entering Grade 10, completed high school (2011-2012 to 2015-2016). The high school completion rate reports the percentages of Alberta students in public, separate, francophone, charter, and accredited private schools who, within three and five years of entering Grade 10, received an Alberta High School Diploma; an Alberta High School Equivalency Diploma (GED); a Certificate of High School Achievement for completing Knowledge and Employability courses and the certificate requirements; entered an Alberta post-secondary program or an apprenticeship program; or earned credits in five Grade 12 courses, including one language arts diploma examination course and three other diploma examination courses.", "num_resources": 2, "num_tags": 4, "organization": {"id": "079da4a3-1719-4361-9168-219985d29cf3", "name": "education", "title": "Education", "type": "organization", "description": "", "image_url": "", "created": "2015-05-13T08:55:38.599044", "is_organization": true, "approval_status": "approved", "state": "active"}, "owner_org": "079da4a3-1719-4361-9168-219985d29cf3", "private": false, "sensitivity": "unrestricted", "source_type": "", "spatialcoverage1": "Alberta", "state": "active", "time_coverage_from": "2011-09-01", "time_coverage_to": "2016-08-31", "title": "High School Completion Rate of Students within 3 Years and within 5 Years of Entering Grade 10, Alberta", "topic": ["Education - Early Childhood to Grade 12"], "type": "opendata", "updatefrequency": "Annual", "url": null, "usage": "Data for this measure are from Alberta Education and Alberta Advanced Education systems. The provincial rate is calculated by dividing the number of high school completers by the number of students in the Grade 10 Cohort, adjusted for attrition, as shown in the formula below: \r\n(High School Completers)/((Grade 10 Cohort-Attrition Factor))=High School Completion Rate\r\n\r\nAttrition is the estimate of the number of students from the Grade 10 Cohort who leave the province or die in the years subsequent to the start of Grade 10. The attrition estimate is based on the following factors: a) mortality; b) emigration; c) interprovincial out migration; d) an estimate of the percentage of 16-, 17-, and 18-year-olds who are enrolled in school (school participation rate); and e) a downward adjustment to account for youth who are not in school. The source of the statistics for deaths, emigrants, inter-provincial out-migrants and population by age (for calculation of attrition and school participation rates) is Statistics Canada, Annual Demographic Estimates.\r\nIn 2010, high school completion rate methodology was revised to reflect new data received from the post-secondary system. Under the revised methodology, the calculations incorporate the post-secondary Classification of Instructional Programs (CIP) coding to better identify those students enrolled in programs that are not deemed to be post-secondary level programming (e.g., academic upgrading). Students in these kinds of programs are not considered completers for the purpose of this measure. Historical results have been revised to reflect this change. The tracking of Grade 10 students excludes some students, such as those identified as having a severe or moderate cognitive disability or a severe multiple disability. \r\nMore information on the methodology can be found in the related document of \r\nStudent Outcomes Measures \u2013 Based on the Grade 10 Cohort.\r\n", "version": null, "resources": [{"cache_last_updated": null, "cache_url": null, "created": "2015-08-17T12:59:42.222816", "datastore_active": true, "description": "", "format": "CSV", "hash": "", "id": "a8864ca1-077c-4ff6-b10e-d4f2af7d72e1", "last_modified": "2018-05-04T17:23:27.389264", "metadata_modified": "2026-03-09T19:46:35.661292", "mimetype": null, "mimetype_inner": null, "name": "CSV", "package_id": "80968b69-c17e-4f26-92c5-eae3b7793ce0", "position": 0, "resource_type": null, "size": null, "state": "active", "url": "https://open.alberta.ca/dataset/80968b69-c17e-4f26-92c5-eae3b7793ce0/resource/a8864ca1-077c-4ff6-b10e-d4f2af7d72e1/download/hsc-5-year-and-3-year.csv", "url_type": "upload"}, {"cache_last_updated": null, "cache_url": null, "created": "2015-08-17T12:59:57.073593", "datastore_active": false, "description": "", "format": "PDF", "hash": "", "id": "321401a9-85f1-4892-a596-7673157feeb8", "last_modified": "2018-05-04T17:24:02.898203", "metadata_modified": "2015-08-17T12:59:57.073593", "mimetype": null, "mimetype_inner": null, "name": "Alberta Official Statistic Visualization", "package_id": "80968b69-c17e-4f26-92c5-eae3b7793ce0", "position": 1, "resource_type": null, "size": null, "state": "active", "url": "https://open.alberta.ca/dataset/80968b69-c17e-4f26-92c5-eae3b7793ce0/resource/321401a9-85f1-4892-a596-7673157feeb8/download/highschoolcompletionrateonepage-03-28-2018.pdf", "url_type": "upload"}], "tags": [{"display_name": "AOS", "id": "c9f208e1-0633-41c9-9383-5f4e42160625", "name": "AOS", "state": "active", "vocabulary_id": null}, {"display_name": "Alberta Official Statistics", "id": "7569743c-c473-4c70-ba4e-24b1f71d84d0", "name": "Alberta Official Statistics", "state": "active", "vocabulary_id": null}, {"display_name": "cohort tracking", "id": "75e6160b-726f-49d2-a198-f91f818b5b96", "name": "cohort tracking", "state": "active", "vocabulary_id": null}, {"display_name": "high school completion rates", "id": "bfb06a8e-c123-4fd7-b7f2-a10087d47481", "name": "high school completion rates", "state": "active", "vocabulary_id": null}], "groups": [], "relationships_as_subject": [], "relationships_as_object": []}, {"archivedate": "2026-08-31", "audience": ["Educators"], "author": null, "author_email": null, "createdate": "1993-01-01 00:00:00", "creator": ["Education"], "creator_user_id": "d11d4737-7afa-424f-a6d2-a8a4c6af917c", "date_modified": "1993-01-01 00:00:00", "id": "80f77b5e-6742-4f1e-a652-1d09c8707674", "identifier-ISBN-print": "0773211519", "isopen": true, "issuedate": "1993-01-01", "language": ["en-CA [default]"], "license_id": "OGLA", "license_title": "Open Government Licence - Alberta", "license_url": "https://open.alberta.ca/licence", "maintainer": null, "maintainer_email": null, "metadata_created": "2026-08-31T20:36:00.081181", "metadata_modified": "2026-08-31T20:36:09.292342", "name": "study-to-identify-and-measure-desirable-student-social-outcomes", "notes": "This report outlines one school jurisdiction's efforts to develop a set of social skills, behaviors, attitude indicators and standards that can be used to assess the quality of a selected portion of that district's educational program and delivery. It describes the development of an expanded systems model of social competence, the use of standardized instruments, and finally the development of a three-level approach to measuring and reporting social skills development.", "num_resources": 1, "num_tags": 3, "organization": {"id": "079da4a3-1719-4361-9168-219985d29cf3", "name": "education", "title": "Education", "type": "organization", "description": "", "image_url": "", "created": "2015-05-13T08:55:38.599044", "is_organization": true, "approval_status": "approved", "state": "active"}, "owner_org": "079da4a3-1719-4361-9168-2199